# Files tracked on dev that must NEVER reach the public repo.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repository root. Blank lines and lines
# beginning with '#' are ignored. Paths are matched exactly, not as globs --
# a glob would make it too easy to exclude something by accident.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The two-remote split assumed a simple invariant: anything tracked on `dev`
# becomes public at the next release, so internal files are never tracked on
# dev. That invariant failed. On 2026-08-24 the public repo was found to be
# carrying, on all 20 refs back to v0.2.0:
#
#   - three AI-generated mock JSS referee reports, formatted as genuine
#     correspondence from "The Editors, Journal of Statistical Software";
#   - docs/CROSS_PROJECT_SYNC.md, which publishes the lab's venue pipeline --
#     papers, target journals, status and deadlines -- for papers bound for
#     blind review, and which CLAUDE.md's own labgraph block withholds
#     precisely because this repository is public;
#   - docs/COMMERCIALIZATION_BRAINSTORM.md, covering commercialization and
#     university IP;
#   - 28 SMJ-paper simulation artifacts sitting inside R/, including a .docx.
#
# Public history was rewritten to remove them. The artifacts were untracked
# from dev outright. The files listed below are different: they are worth
# versioning privately but must not ship, so they stay tracked on dev and are
# dropped at snapshot time instead.
#
# The invariant is no longer "trust that nobody tracked the wrong thing". It
# is checked: tools/check_public_snapshot.R fails the release if any path here
# survives into a snapshot, and CLAUDE.md's release recipe runs it at step 3.
#
# Adding a path here is a deliberate act. If a file is not worth versioning at
# all, gitignore it instead -- this list is only for content that has private
# value.

